.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_unset_trap(bc_client_t *c, const char *signal);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a signal trap from the bash\-server session associated with the
client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
After a successful call, the signal reverts to its default disposition
(the behavior it had before any trap was set for it).
.PP
The function sends an \f[CR]unset\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace
\f[CR]\(dqtrap\(dq\f[R] and the given signal name.
The server performs the equivalent of \f[CR]trap \- signal\f[R] in the
shell session, which resets the signal handler to its default action.
.PP
If no trap is set for the specified signal, the server treats this as a
successful operation (no error is returned).
.PP
Signal names follow the same conventions as
\f[CR]bc_state_set_trap()\f[R]: they may include or omit the
\f[CR]SIG\f[R] prefix and are case\-insensitive.
